-- title:
--   Branch valuation rings of X₁(Mp) are unramified over A
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M \ge 5$ be a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ (Laurent series over $L$) which is equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the field of $q$-expansions of modular functions for $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an algebra structure over $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A \to L$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be a nonzero element whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of $q^{-1}$ times the power series $\mathrm{jNumQ}$, the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant. Let $\varpi \in A$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $V$ be a valuation subring of $K$ such that the image of $A$ lies in $V$, the image of every element of the maximal ideal of $A$ is a non-unit of $V$, and for every polynomial $P \in A[X]$ whose reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ is nonzero, both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $V$. Then every non-unit $f$ of $V$ can be written as $f = \varpi g$ with $g \in V$; that is, the maximal ideal of $V$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$.
--
--   The assertion is that such valuation rings of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $L$ — the local rings at the generic points of the special fibre of the integral model over the discrete valuation ring $A \subset L = \mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ — are unramified over $A$, so that $\varpi$ remains a uniformiser and the special fibre is reduced at its generic points; adjoining $\zeta_p$ is what makes this hold. It is used in the project to prove reducedness of the pullback of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ and unramifiedness of its charts, and in the corresponding analysis for the Hecke correspondence.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_eq_mul_of_mem_nonunits_valuationSubring_x1_mul.lean

